  "observed_side_effects": [
    "Real SkillTool invocation loads the qualified command skill and records literal invocation arguments; unsupported template syntax is never evaluated.",
    "The generated file is persisted under the host config parent/cache/plugin-commands/<content-and-identity-hash>/<name>/SKILL.md. Cache identity includes original root, source path, plugin identity and exact rendered bytes.",
    "Same command in two marketplaces has different physical cache paths and verified original provenance; disabling one package removes only its contribution.",
    "All distinct sources in a slug collision are rejected, including an oversize candidate. Logical .codex-plugin/migrated-command-skills root ordering determines clashes with ordinary package skills.",
    "The existing configured Markdown security audit is applied to source templates and the normal directory audit is applied to generated skills. No command frontmatter can add tool permissions.",
    "Redirected or tampered cache paths produce explicit diagnostics. Existing cache entries are verified, not overwritten. Changes in source content yield a different immutable cache key."
  ],
  "intentional_layout_and_safety_differences": [
    "The reference writes migrated skills into the package at install time. This host lazily derives them into its own cache to preserve original package bytes, retaining reference logical root precedence. Relative template text is not rewritten or given an implicit resource mirror.",
    "Shared plugin path auditing refuses parent components, root aliases and symlinks; an unsafe or missing explicit command root rejects that command inventory while unrelated healthy package skills remain independently available.",
    "Rejected sources produce path-scoped diagnostics rather than silently disappearing. Configured host safety restrictions remain authoritative.",
    "No brand replacement is performed. Only the plugin migration profile document filename normalization is retained."
  ],
